{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetLKMjzDRCb3RtskYhtB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough context. Let me summarize my analysis findings:\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that confirms shipments, transitioning them from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED`, handling retries idempotently, rejecting `CANCELLED` shipments with 409, and rejecting unknown shipments with 404.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model and status enum: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27`\n- ShipmentController: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20`\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository with save/findById: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27`\n- Exception classes: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:19-24` (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException)\n- ErrorCode enum: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37`\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28`\n- Existing tests: `src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt`\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Controllers use `@RestController` and `@RequestMapping` annotations\n2. Endpoints return `ResponseEntity<T>` for success cases\n3. Error handling via exceptions: `ConflictException` (409), `ResourceNotFoundException` (404)\n4. All error codes defined in the `ErrorCode` enum\n5. GlobalExceptionHandler converts ApiExceptions to ApiError envelopes automatically\n6. Tests use MockMvc with status() and jsonPath() assertions\n7. Repository @BeforeEach resets state between tests\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` - Must add new ErrorCode for CANCELLED state case\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` - Must add POST confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Must add tests for all confirm scenarios\n\n**Risks:**\n1. If the new ErrorCode breaks API compatibility (though it's an addition, not a change)\n2. If status transition logic is incorrect, idempotency could fail\n3. If repository mutation doesn't persist, changes could be lost\n\n**Open questions:** None identified that change correctness.\n\nNow moving to the design phase.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n**File 1: ApiError.kt**\n- Add `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` error code to the enum for the case where a shipment is already cancelled and cannot be confirmed\n\n**File 2: ShipmentController.kt**\n- Add new endpoint: `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`\n- Logic:\n  1. Fetch the shipment by ID; throw `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found\n  2. Check the current status:\n     - If `CREATED`: update status to `CONFIRMED`, save, and return the updated shipment with HTTP 200\n     - If `CONFIRMED`: return the shipment unchanged with HTTP 200 (idempotent)\n     - If `CANCELLED`: throw `ConflictException` with the new `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` error code\n  3. Return `ResponseEntity` with status 200 and body as the (updated or unchanged) shipment\n\n**File 3: ShipmentControllerTest.kt**\n- Add test: confirm a CREATED shipment -> transitions to CONFIRMED (200)\n- Add test: confirm a CREATED shipment twice -> second call succeeds and changes nothing (idempotent)\n- Add test: confirm a CANCELLED shipment -> 409 with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED error code\n- Add test: confirm unknown shipment -> 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Alternative: Avoid adding a new ErrorCode and use VALIDATION_FAILED instead\n  - Rejected because VALIDATION_FAILED semantically means input validation, not state validation; adding a specific error code is clearer to API clients and follows the existing pattern\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED)**\n   - Input: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (no body)\n   - Repository lookup: findById(\"S-1\") returns Shipment with status=CREATED\n   - Update: Create new Shipment with status=CONFIRMED, save to repository\n   - Output: 200 OK with Shipment JSON body\n\n2. **Idempotent path (CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED)**\n   - Input: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (no body)\n   - Repository lookup: findById(\"S-1\") returns Shipment with status=CONFIRMED\n   - No update: Return the same Shipment unchanged\n   - Output: 200 OK with Shipment JSON body\n\n3. **Cancelled error (CANCELLED → Error)**\n   - Input: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (no body)\n   - Repository lookup: findById(\"S-1\") returns Shipment with status=CANCELLED\n   - Throw: ConflictException with ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_CANCELLED\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler catches it, returns 409 with ApiError envelope\n\n4. **Not found error (Unknown ID)**\n   - Input: POST /shipments/S-unknown/confirm (no body)\n   - Repository lookup: findById(\"S-unknown\") returns null\n   - Throw: ResourceNotFoundException with ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler catches it, returns 404 with ApiError envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Confirm CREATED shipment → 200, status changes to CONFIRMED\n- Test 2: Confirm CONFIRMED shipment (idempotent) → 200, status remains CONFIRMED\n- Test 3: Confirm CANCELLED shipment → 409 with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED error code\n- Test 4: Confirm non-existent shipment → 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":527,"cache_read_input_tokens":21844,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":527},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae8576ad-a1c7-4399-9244-30b799407121","uuid":"445543ea-f754-4790-be4c-290ffa74666b","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:25:00.426Z","request_id":"req_011CetLKM5J8quWhZ9n1Wavt"}
